# Resolve known native vehicle blockers before presentation review

Track known vehicle defects that still prevent complete source-faithful native
vehicle construction. These are implementation blockers, not requests for
manual visual tuning.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Construct vehicle render geometry and rig directly from normalized JSON
  without an FBX import prerequisite.
- [ ] Preserve authored wheel geometry while replacing temporary spherical wheel
  collision assumptions with the exact accepted native tire and suspension
  representation.
- [ ] Translate authored articulated joint semantics for doors, hood, and trunk
  instead of leaving secondary bodies permanently kinematic.
- [ ] Recreate source-backed reflective `spheremap`, glass, wheel, and remaining
  material families without inventing PBR values or fallback textures.
- [ ] Bind all source-backed vehicle material slots so missing presentation is
  explicit and no slot silently falls back to Unreal's default material.
- [ ] Preserve the proven vehicle basis with forward `+X`, right `+Y`, and up
  `+Z` through native construction rather than FBX root rotations or mirrors.
- [ ] Keep vehicle self-collision and source joint policy deterministic and
  verified against normalized physics evidence.
- [ ] Retest steering, braking, suspension, damage, articulated parts, cameras,
  and runtime stability after the native asset path replaces FBX.

